      "id": "about",
      "type": "layout.comment",
      "name": "Original shadow and defect fixtures - MIT",
      "description": "Original synthetic images, truth, generator and projects: repository MIT. Run all: clear.png has no shadow candidates and retains the 48-pixel dark defect. shadow.png has exactly 9,984 shadow pixels (x < 104), attenuation 0.5 and gain 2. Both corrected outputs equal the independent clear.png pixel for pixel, including the sharp part boundary, cast-shadow boundary, texture and real dark defect. Defect contrast against the nominal reference remains R/G/B = 8000/7000/6000. Minimum shadow area 256 rejects the smaller isolated defect in the clear frame. The reference supplies a robust regional gain, never replacement image pixels. Invalid_fit.json has joined attenuation 0.4/0.7 and must withhold Image/Gain. This is a neutral constant-attenuation hypothesis; similar dark material changes can be confused with shadows. Use trusted Fit mask support and validate your job. No registration, penumbra model or final inspection judgment is implied. API: https://docs.opencv.org/5.0/main_modules/imgproc_shape.html",
